2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Ghostty engine embedding: `ghostty_app_set_color_scheme`/`ghostty_surface_set_color_scheme` only flip `ConditionalState.theme` and fire a `.reload_config{soft:true}` action; nothing re-derives the config automatically — `GhosttyRuntimeAdapter.handleAction` doesn't handle `GHOSTTY_ACTION_RELOAD_CONFIG`, so adopting the native `theme=dark:X,light:Y` syntax would require new engine-callback-reentrant code, not just emitting two names.
   - SwiftUI `@Observable`/`ObservableObject` invalidation-storm pattern (WORKROOM-2B): established fix is stripping observation from rows, hoisting values/closures to the parent, adding `Equatable` + `.equatable()` at the `ForEach` call site, switching `VStack`→`LazyVStack` only for fixed-height rows.
   - `#if DEBUG static var bodyPasses`/`lastCommittedResult` counters as the standard measurement/regression-observation seam pattern in this codebase.
   - Swift Concurrency: `withTaskCancellationHandler`, `TimeoutCancelBox` (NSLock-guarded, handles onCancel firing before/during/after attach), `TimeoutGate.settle` (exactly-once continuation resume guard), unstructured `Task<T, Never>` not propagating cancellation from a parent `.task(id:)` (root cause of the Avatar staleness bug).
   - `GitStatusReading`/`JJStatusReading` protocol seams mirroring `StatusCommandRunning`'s injection role for native (non-CLI) VCS reads.
   - `combinedWorkingDiff`: combining a file's `.index` (HEAD→index) and `.workingTree` (index→worktree) status deltas into one HEAD→worktree diff, mirroring the existing `.conflicted` case's blob-lookup technique.
   - `gitFormat`'s `type: Diff.DeltaType` parameter controls ONLY which side (`---`/`+++`) renders as `/dev/null` — `.added`/`.untracked` ⇒ no old side, `.deleted` ⇒ no new side — independent of the patch's actual hunk content; deriving this from the WRONG delta's `.type` produces a self-contradictory diff.
   - LRU vs FIFO cache eviction: `AvatarImageLoader`'s `cacheOrder` array was insertion-ordered with eviction via `removeFirst()`, but cache HITS never re-ordered the entry — genuinely FIFO despite class-doc claims of LRU.
   - `.task(id:)` cancellation semantics: SwiftUI cancels the old `Task` when `id` changes, but that cancellation must be explicitly checked (`Task.isCancelled`) after any `await` before committing a result — otherwise a stale, slow fetch can silently overwrite a newer view's state.
   - `StatusCommandRunning`/`GitStatusReading` counting test doubles + `InFlightCounter` pattern for asserting `withTaskGroup`-bounded concurrency caps.
   - gstack `/review` skill machinery: specialist subagent dispatch (testing/maintainability/performance/security/etc.), Claude adversarial subagent, Codex `exec`/`review` adversarial + structured passes, cross-model finding synthesis, Fix-First Review (AUTO-FIX vs ASK classification), fingerprint-based dedup, confidence calibration (1-10 scale with a pre-emit "quote the motivating line" verification gate).
